        <briefdescription>
<para>Generic getter function template for value retrieval. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type from which the value is to be retrieved.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>t</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The object or value to be accessed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The value obtained via the relevant getter implementation.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput>get</computeroutput> function template retrieves the value from the provided object or type. If the type provides a <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a0c9d0a57b84d040bb1dcedd9d7130825" kindref="member">get()</ref></computeroutput> member function, it is invoked; otherwise the argument itself is returned unchanged.</para>
<para>The selection is performed at compile time using <computeroutput>if constexpr</computeroutput> and an inline <computeroutput>requires</computeroutput> expression, superseding the classic two-overload SFINAE technique used prior to C++20.</para>
<para>All definitions are intended for internal use within the framework and are implemented in the <computeroutput>include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus</computeroutput> folder to maintain a structured and modular codebase. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
